<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maxixcatzin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1520</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maxixcatzin was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ocotelolco">Ocotelolco</a>, the most powerful of the four altepetl that made up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> state of Tlaxcala, at the time of the Spanish arrival. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlaxcalans">Tlaxcalans</a> fought Cortés in 1519, he argued for alliance with the Spanish and supported them after their flight from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> in 1520, but he died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maxixcatzin.jpg" alt="Maxixcatzin" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thelmadatter · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MaxixcatzinTlaxRegMus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
